# Pre-flight reachability/feasibility check for a pose target.
# Implemented by arm_api2 (moveit2_simple_iface) using IK + planning-scene
# collision check against the current robot state. Designed to be cheap
# (~50 ms) so the GUI can batch-check several grasp candidates before
# committing to a plan, eliminating the 5 s × N OMPL timeout loop.

# Pose to check, in PLANNING_FRAME (or any frame TF can resolve to it).
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped pose

# Optional: number of IK seeds to try. 0 => server default.
uint8 ik_attempts

# Optional: per-attempt IK timeout in seconds. 0.0 => server default.
float64 ik_timeout_sec
---
# True if at least one collision-free IK solution exists for `pose`.
bool reachable

# True if the resolved goal state collides (self or environment) with the
# current planning scene. When `reachable == true`, this is always false.
bool in_collision

# How many distinct IK seeds produced a valid solution (capped to ik_attempts).
uint8 ik_solutions_found

# Human-readable explanation; safe to surface in the GUI.
string reason
